{
  "abstract": "For a four-point support in Z/nZ with n positive, the complete labelled ordered-square fibre has cardinality one, two or four. At most two fixed binary membership probes separate that fibre. The full square and its fibre are supplied; no computational runtime bound or adaptive query lower bound is asserted.",
